Fillets: the order of the analytic pieces of a closed rounding (mitcad#133).

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart sorts the pieces SplitKPart cuts out of
an analytic blend of a periodic spine (a torus along a whole circle whose
contact line on a face leaves that face several times) by their start on
the spine. The exchange sort kept the j-th piece read before the inner loop
and swapped that stale piece in at every later exchange, so a list whose
second piece belonged at the end (the piece that closes the circle) came
out with that piece repeated and others lost. The walks between the pieces
then went over the repeated piece again and the stripe failed in
PerformSetOfKGen (ChFiDS_CommonPoint::Vector on a point without a tangent),
on a rounding of a circle whose contact on a plane crosses six slots. The
j-th piece is now read again at each step.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -3587,9 +3587,10 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart(occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>& Stripe, const
         }
         for (int j = 1; j < nbsd; j++)
         {
-          occ::handle<ChFiDS_SurfData> jSD = LSD.Value(j);
           for (int k = j + 1; k <= nbsd; k++)
           {
+            // The j-th SurfData is read again at each step: a swap replaces it.
+            occ::handle<ChFiDS_SurfData> jSD = LSD.Value(j);
             occ::handle<ChFiDS_SurfData> kSD = LSD.Value(k);
             double                       jwf = jSD->FirstSpineParam();
             jwf                              = ChFi3d_InPeriod(jwf, wfp, wlp, tolesp);
